schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Tax Implications of Cryptocurrency
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A US-centric primer on crypto taxation: crypto is treated as property
    (not currency), cost basis, short-vs-long-term capital gains, taxable vs
    non-taxable events, NFT and DeFi-specific tax treatment, gas-fee
    handling, record-keeping needs, and the relevant IRS forms (8949,
    Schedule D, Schedule 1, 1099-DA).
  audience: individuals/organisations transacting in crypto in the US
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      The article flags its own biggest uncertainty: whether NFTs count as
      "collectibles" taxed at 28% is explicitly called "debated," with a
      "consult a pro if unsure" caveat.
  related_concepts:
    - capital-gains-crypto
  related_resources:
    - cointracker
    - koinly
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  high_risk: true
  public_use: not-public-yet
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/tax-implications.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    high_risk: true — this article gives jurisdiction-specific tax/legal
    guidance (a high-risk trigger category per ingest rules); see
    accompanying public-use-boundary. The article itself carries an explicit
    disclaimer: "Educational purposes only. Not tax advice."
